From e58c83cdd2c6b860982c3d35eaeb5b7940c57425 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:36:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp P2] TR-098 LAN branch in C for the MTK SDK

Ports phase P2 of the data model off the easycwmp shell library and into C,
70 parameters over four modules that the registry merges into one LANDevice:

  lan_mtk.c        LANDevice.1 counters, transmit power, and the whole
                   LANHostConfigManagement subtree with IPInterface.1
  lanhosts_mtk.c   Hosts.Host.{i} browsed from the product's UCI "lanhost",
                   lease time still read from /tmp/dhcp.leases
  laneth_mtk.c     LANEthernetInterfaceConfig.{i} and .Stats, four ports,
                   counters from /proc/tc3162/gsw_stats and the port netdev
  x_ais_mesh_mtk.c X_AIS_Mesh, the operator's forced-inform mesh object

Same UCI options, same reload commands and the same fault codes as the shell
functions they replace, including dhcp.lan.configurable refusing writes with
9002 everywhere but MaxAddress, which answers 9007.  Service reloads and the
mesh reboot are queued on the apply-service list so they run after the engine
commits, which is what the shell got from committing inline.

dmmtk gains mtk_uci_default() ($UCI_GET_DEFAULT, the /rom factory tree),
mtk_ipv4_parse()/mtk_ipv4_str() and mtk_file_write().

Parameter names verified against the product tree: 70 of 70, no extras.
NOT build tested: no compiler in this environment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
